From: M5 measurement campaign (2026-07-28/29 evening, session c0b61ee1)
Subject: [PATCH] eval_fair_puct: bare `--smoke` crashes on args.games=None

STATUS: NOT APPLIED to the M5 campaign runs. Filed for the morning merge.
        Both M5 cells were smoked by passing `--games N` explicitly, so the
        harness ran BYTE-UNMODIFIED and neither cell carries a code divergence.

FOUND: 2026-07-28, first results-bearing use of this harness on darwin-arm64.
       The defect is PLATFORM-INDEPENDENT — it reproduces on Linux too.

WHAT:  `_smoke()` reads `args.games`, which argparse defaults to None. The
       `--games` -> `--n` alias is resolved in main() (`if args.games is not
       None: args.n = args.games`) but that assignment goes the OTHER way and
       leaves args.games itself None. So any invocation of `--smoke` WITHOUT an
       explicit `--games` dies before playing a single game:

           File ".../eval_fair_puct.py", line 1814, in _smoke
             for i in range(max(1, args.games)):
         TypeError: '>' not supported between instances of 'NoneType' and 'int'

FIX:   fall back to ONE game. Deliberately not `args.n`: a smoke is a wiring
       proof, and args.n defaults to 100 — inheriting that would turn a smoke
       into a ~2-hour run at production knobs.

APPLY: git apply scripts/m5_bench/patches/0001-eval_fair_puct-bare-smoke-games-none.patch

Verified against eval_fair_puct.py at code_rev cc73b3cc25325a0754835be050afbe040e8c6197.
---
 scripts/classical_search/eval_fair_puct.py | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/classical_search/eval_fair_puct.py b/scripts/classical_search/eval_fair_puct.py
--- a/scripts/classical_search/eval_fair_puct.py
+++ b/scripts/classical_search/eval_fair_puct.py
@@ -1811,7 +1811,13 @@
     import random
     results = []
     t0 = time.perf_counter()
-    for i in range(max(1, args.games)):
+    # `--games` is the OPTIONAL alias for `--n` (resolved into args.n in main(), but
+    # left as None here when the caller did not pass it). Reading it raw made a bare
+    # `--smoke` crash with TypeError: '>' not supported between NoneType and int.
+    # Fall back to a SINGLE game -- a smoke is a wiring proof, not an eval, so it must
+    # NOT inherit args.n's default of 100.
+    _n_smoke = args.games if args.games is not None else 1
+    for i in range(max(1, _n_smoke)):
         a_seat = i % 2
         seed = args.seed_start + (i // 2)
         random.seed(seed)
